#import "../../../proofs.typ": speech, footnote

== 2. Of the Holy Ghost

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 52]: What believest thou concerning the Holy Ghost?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: First, that He is true and Coeternal God, with the#footnote[Gen 1:2; Isa 48:16; 1 Cor 3:16; 1 Cor 6:19; Acts 5:3–4] eternal Father, and the Son; secondly, that he is#footnote[Matt 28:19; 2 Cor 1:2] also given unto me, to make#footnote[Gal 3:14; 1 Pet 1:2; 1 Cor 6:17] me, through a true Faith, Partaker of Christ and all his Benefits, to#footnote[Acts 9:31] comfort me, and to#footnote[John 14:16; 1 Pet 4:14] abide with me for ever.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 53]: What believest thou concerning the Holy and Catholick Church of Christ?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: I believe that the Son#footnote[\[No reference printed in 1680\]] of God doth from#footnote[\[No reference printed in 1680\]] the beginning of the#footnote[\[No reference printed in 1680\]] World to the End thereof, gather,#footnote[Isa 59:21; Eph 5:26] defend, and preserve unto himself by his Spirit#footnote[Acts 2:4, 42; Eph 4:3–6] and Word, out of#footnote[Matt 16:18] whole Mankind, a#footnote[1 John 3:21; 2 Cor 13:5] Company chosen to everlasting Life, and agreeing in true Faith; and that I am a lively Member of that Company, and so shal#footnote[\[No reference printed in 1680\]] remain for ever.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 54]: What mean those words, The Communion of Saints?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: First, that all and every one who believeth, are in#footnote[1 John 1:3; Rom 8:32; 1 Cor 1:2; 12:13; 1 Cor 6:17] common Partakers of Christ and all his Graces, as being his Members; and then that every one ought#footnote[1 Cor 12:21; Phil 2:4–6] readily and chearfully to bestow the Gifts and Graces which they have received to the common Commodity and Safety of all.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 55]: What believest thou concerning Remission of Sins?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That God, for the Satisfaction made by Christ,#footnote[1 John 2:2; 2 Cor 5:19, 21] hath put out all the#footnote[Jer 31:34; Ps 103:3–4; Ps 10:11; Rom 7:24–25; Rom 8:1–3] Remembrance of my Sins, and also of that Corruption within me wherewith I must fight all my life time, and doth freely indow me with the Righteousness of Christ, that I come not at any#footnote[John 3:18] time into Judgment.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 56]: What Comfort hast thou by the Resurrection of the Flesh?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That not only my Soul, after it shall depart out of my Body, shall#footnote[Luke 23:43; Phil 1:23] presently be taken up to Christ, but that this my Flesh also, being raised up by the Power of Christ, shall be again united to my Soul, and#footnote[1 Cor 15:53; Job 19:25–26; 1 John 3:2; Phil 3:21] shall be made like to the glorious Body of Christ.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 57]: What Comfort takest thou of the Article of everlasting Life?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That forasmuch#footnote[2 Cor 5:1–3] as I feel already in my Heart the beginning of everlasting Life,#footnote[1 Cor 2:9; John 17:3] it shall at length come to pass that after this Life I shall enjoy full and perfect Bliss, wherein I may magnify God for ever, which Blessedness verily neither Eye hath seen, nor Ear heard, neither hath any Man in thought conceived it.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 58]: But when thou believest all these things, what profit redoundeth thence unto thee?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That I am righteous in Christ before God, and an Heir#footnote[Rom 1:17; John 3:36; Rom 3:4, 22, 24–25, 28; Rom 5:1; Gal 2:16; Eph 2:8–9] of eternal Life.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 59]: How art thou righteous before God?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Only by Faith in Christ Jesus. So that although my Concience accuse me that I have grievously trespassed against all the Commandments of God, and have not#footnote[Rom 3:9,&c] kept one of them, and further am as yet#footnote[Rom 7:23] prone to all Evil; yet notwithstanding if#footnote[Rom 3:22; John 3:18] I embrace these Benefits of Christ with a true Confidence and Perswasion of mind, the full and#footnote[Titus 3:5; Eph 2:8–9] perfect Satisfaction, Righteousness and Holiness of Christ, without any#footnote[1 John 2:2] Merit of Mine, of the#footnote[Rom 3:24; Deut 9:5–6; Ezek 36:22] meer Mercy#footnote[1 John 2:1,&c] of God is#footnote[Rom 4:4–5; 2 Cor 5:19] imputed and given unto me, and that so, as if neither I had committed any Sin, neither any Corruption did stick unto me; yea as if I my#footnote[2 Cor 5:21] self had perfectly accomplished that Obedience which Christ accomplished for me.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 60]: Why affirmest thou that thou art made Righteous by Faith only?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Not for that I please God through the Worthiness of meer Faith, but because only the Satisfaction, Righteousness and Holiness of Christ is my Righteousness#footnote[1 Cor 1:30,&c; 1 Cor 2:2] before God, and#footnote[1 John 5:10] I cannot take hold of it, or apply it unto my self any other way than by Faith.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 61]: Why cannot our good Works be Righteousness, or some part of Righteousness before God?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: Because that Righteousness which must stand fast before the Judgment of God, must be in all Points perfect#footnote[Gal 3:10; Deut 27:26] and agreeable to the Law of God. Now our Works, even the best of them, are imperfect in this Life, and#footnote[Isa 64:6] defiled with Sin.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 62]: How is it that our good Works merit nothing, seeing God promiseth that he will give a Reward for them both in this Life, and in the Life to come?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: That Reward is not given of merit,#footnote[Luke 17:10] but of Grace.]

#speech[#smallcaps[Question 63]: But doth not this Doctrine make Men careless and profain?]

#speech[#smallcaps[Answer]: No, For neither can it be but they who are incorporated into Christ through Faith, should bring forth the#footnote[Matt 7:18; John 15:5] Fruits of Thankfulness.]
